# Normalise every text file to LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with the default core.autocrlf=true gets CRLF
# on disk, and the docs drift check compares a CRLF file on disk against the LF
# text the generator produces. It reported docs/rules.md as out of date on both
# Windows runners while being byte identical in the repository, which is a
# failure that tells a contributor to regenerate a file that is already correct.
#
# Binary fixtures are listed explicitly so nothing here can corrupt them.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.tgz binary
*.gz binary
